@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Notice";
    // EDIT THIS: the email people can use to reach your team about their data
    var contactEmail = "your-team-email@example.com";
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <h1 class="h2 fw-bold">Privacy Notice</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">
            Dwellr is a student pilot project. This notice explains how we handle your personal
            information, in line with the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173). Last updated: November 2026.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
            Your name, email address and password (stored in a protected form we cannot read), your role
            (tenant or landlord), and a mobile number if you ask us to list a property. If you join the waitlist,
            your budget, occupation and preferred area. We also keep the property details and photos landlords post,
            messages sent through the app, listing reports, and demo wallet records.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
            To run the pilot: create your account, contact you about the pilot, connect renters with landlords,
            verify landlords, and handle reports of suspicious listings. The wallet is a demo and uses no real money.
            By registering or submitting a form, you agree to this use of your information.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who can see it</h2>
        <p>
            Only the Dwellr team and our hosting provider can access stored data. Tenants and landlords can see each
            other's name when they message each other or complete a rental. A listing's street address is shown only to
            the landlord and to people who have messaged them. We do not sell your information.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Landlord verification</h2>
        @* Confirm this matches reality: do you keep any ID copies outside the app? *@
        <p>
            Our team verifies landlords by contacting them directly. The app does not accept or store ID uploads.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
            We keep your information while the pilot runs. When the pilot ends, we delete it, or sooner if you ask us to.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">How we protect it</h2>
        <p>
            Passwords are stored in a protected form, only the Dwellr team can open the admin pages, and messages are
            visible only to the people in the conversation. No system is perfectly secure, so please do not share
            sensitive details such as card or ID numbers in messages.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
            You can ask to see, correct, or delete your information, object to how we use it, or withdraw your consent
            at any time. Email us at <a href="mailto:@contactEmail">@contactEmail</a>. If you think we handled your
            information wrongly, you can file a complaint with the
            <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Privacy Commission</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>